<title>FRANCE: Chirac, Kohl end talks without statement.</title>
<headline>Chirac, Kohl end talks without statement.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French President Jacques Chirac and German Chancellor Helmut Kohl ended a three-hour meeting on European Union reform on Tuesday without making a statement.</p>
<p>While they were meeting a bomb exploded in a Paris underground train killing two people and injuring 47. French officials said Chirac was being briefed on the attack and did not wish to make any statement in the meantime.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
